cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this repository, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: >-
  IndicAlignProbe: a paired English / Romanized-Hindi safety-asymmetry
  evaluation harness for open-weight language models
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bibek-nagpal/Indic-LLM-Safety"
version: "0.1.0"

# Individual author names are deliberately omitted while the associated
# manuscript is under double-blind review. Replace this entity entry with the
# per-person `given-names` / `family-names` records once the work is
# de-anonymised; do not add names here before then.
authors:
  - name: "The IndicAlignProbe authors"

abstract: >-
  A reproducible harness and frozen evidence archive for measuring whether an
  open-weight language model assists with the same request differently when it
  is written in English versus Romanized Hindi (Hinglish). The measured
  construct is non-assistance -- a score of 0 on a 0-3 information-assistance
  scale -- rather than refusal. The frozen V2 experiment evaluates 504
  equivalence-certified EN/RH prompt pairs against three target models and
  finds a model-dependent asymmetry rather than a universal one.

keywords:
  - AI safety
  - language models
  - multilingual evaluation
  - Romanized Hindi
  - Hinglish
  - code-switching
  - safety asymmetry
  - reproducibility
